  "subtitle": "Hungarian crescent rolls: soft, enriched, and milk-glazed",
  "excerpt": "Hungarian kifli are soft, crescent-shaped enriched bread rolls made from a milk and egg dough enriched with butter. They are light and tender with a thin, egg-glazed crust and make a gentle, slightly sweet roll for breakfast or alongside soups and stews. Unlike the flaky Austrian kipferl, Hungarian kifli is a yeasted roll rather than a pastry, and it is much softer and more bread-like.",
