  "sourceNotes": "Kifli (also spelled kiflice in the southern Slavic tradition) are crescent rolls eaten across Central Europe, with the Hungarian kifli being a soft, milk-enriched yeasted roll rather than the flaky or walnut-filled versions found in other countries. Hungarian kifli are documented in Hungarian cookery books from the 19th century onward and are still the standard breakfast roll in Hungarian households.",
