  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kifli dough is enriched with egg and butter, which makes it very soft and a pleasure to handle once kneaded. The shaping is straightforward: divide the dough into triangles and roll them up from the wide end. The key to the crescent form is pulling the tips outward after rolling so they curve rather than pointing straight. Bake them pale and soft, not the deep gold you would aim for with a lean roll."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
